{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('map.json'))\nb=[x for x in m['behaviors'] if x['id']=='B15-durable-record'][0]\nb['important_branches'][0]=\\\"the header writes bal at [0:4) and then vbal into the same bytes, and Status at byte [4] before Seq at [5:9); a direct check on this snapshot confirmed that a record produced with distinct field values carries vbal at offset 0 and no bal value at all (claim C2-durable-record-preserves-written-fields, confirmed in scope)\\\"\nb['unknowns']=[\\\"whether any external tool or later revision reads the stable store; no reader exists in the captured snapshot, so the intended offsets are inferred from the writes themselves (S19-durable-record)\\\"]\nf=[x for x in m['facts'] if x['id']=='F7-durable-bytes'][0]\nf['unknowns']=[\\\"the confirmed check for claim C2-durable-record-preserves-written-fields shows the produced record does not carry the value written for bal and places Status inside the bytes a reader would use for vbal; whether an external reader's expected offsets differ from that remains unread\\\"]\nf['representation'].append(\\\"bytes written by Replica.recordInstanceMetadata for one instance with distinct bal, vbal, Status and Seq: 04030201|03|100f0e0d|deps in the confirmed run (vbal at offset 0, no bal)\\\")\nod=m['core_overview']['open_details']\nfor i,o in enumerate(od):\n    if o.startswith('recordInstanceMetadata writes bal and vbal'):\n        od[i]=\\\"recordInstanceMetadata writes bal at [0:4) and then vbal into the same bytes, with Status at byte [4] and Seq at [5:9); the direct check for claim C2-durable-record-preserves-written-fields confirmed in scope that the produced record carries vbal at offset 0 and no bal value, so the ballot context the 